From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:27:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): load history with tool-output previews, fetch
 results on expand

Hydrate the transcript (initial window, scroll-up pages, reconnect
backfill) with `tool_output=preview`, so a history page carries the
head of each long tool result instead of the whole thing. Tool rows
render collapsed; when the reader expands one whose output is a preview
the card asks the store for the full item, which fetches it once via
`GET /v1/sessions/{id}/items/{item_id}` and swaps it into the result
block. The card shows the preview with a loading note meanwhile and a
retry on failure. Results that are rendered as cards from their text
(AskUserQuestion, ExitPlanMode, sys_advise_models) are inflated when the
page is fetched, so those cards never see a cut-off result. Live-streamed
output in the current turn is untouched.

Opening the benchmark session now moves 7 KB on the wire for the
100-item initial window instead of 225 KB, and an expanded result loads
in ~25 ms.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/lean-history-items; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit ef52e265d3cfa53f62ef01dda1f75a11608589b7)
Docs: none (performance: history pages carry tool-output previews and expanding a tool row loads the rest; no setting)
